## SUMMARY

<span lang="en">Cloud applications require scalable processing capacity, flexibility to extend and change functionality, and high availability. Textus/CNCF embeds the complex execution controls supporting these qualities in shared infrastructure, so that development using CML models and standard CNCF facilities can obtain reactive behavior. This guide explains the architecture and combinations of mechanisms that make this division of responsibilities possible.</span><span lang="ja">クラウドアプリケーションには、負荷に応じた処理能力の拡大、機能の拡張や変更への柔軟性、高可用性が求められます。Textus/CNCFは、これらを支える複雑な実行制御を共通基盤に組み込み、CMLのモデルとCNCFの標準機能を使う開発からリアクティブな動作を得られるようにしています。本書では、この分担を実現するアーキテクチャと技術の組合せを説明します。</span>

# Realizing Reactive Qualities through the Whole Architecture｜リアクティブ性を全体アーキテクチャで実現する

<span lang="ja">バックエンドの処理を非同期のメッセージで連携させると、呼出し側と処理側が同時に動作し続ける必要がなくなり、部品ごとに処理能力や配置を調整しやすくなります。この分離に、容量の調整、負荷制御、障害の隔離と回復を組み合わせることで、次の品質改善につながります。</span><span lang="en">Connecting backend processes through asynchronous messages removes the need for callers and receivers to remain active together, making capacity and placement easier to adjust for each component. Combining this separation with capacity adjustment, load control, failure isolation, and recovery supports the following quality improvements.</span>

#+CAPTION: <span lang="ja">表1　リアクティブな構成による品質属性の改善</span><span lang="en">Table 1. Quality improvements supported by reactive architecture</span>

| <span lang="ja">品質属性</span><span lang="en">Quality attribute</span> | <span lang="ja">得られる改善</span><span lang="en">Improvement</span> | <span lang="ja">リアクティブな構成での対応</span><span lang="en">Reactive architectural response</span> |
| --- | --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">スケーラビリティ（処理能力の拡張）</span><span lang="en">Scalability</span> | <span lang="ja">負荷の高い処理の能力を増やしやすい</span><span lang="en">Increase capacity for heavily loaded processing</span> | <span lang="ja">処理を分離し、複数の実行先へ負荷を分散する</span><span lang="en">Separate processing and distribute load across execution instances</span> |
| <span lang="ja">弾力性</span><span lang="en">Elasticity</span> | <span lang="ja">需要の変動に応じて処理能力を調整できる</span><span lang="en">Adjust capacity as demand changes</span> | <span lang="ja">実行数の増減と、下流の容量に応じた受付制御を組み合わせる</span><span lang="en">Combine instance scaling with admission control based on downstream capacity</span> |
| <span lang="ja">高可用性</span><span lang="en">High availability</span> | <span lang="ja">一部が停止してもサービスを継続しやすい</span><span lang="en">Continue service when part of the system stops</span> | <span lang="ja">障害を区画内に抑え、冗長化と実行先の切替えを組み合わせる</span><span lang="en">Contain failures and combine redundancy with routing to available instances</span> |
| <span lang="ja">耐障害性・回復可能性</span><span lang="en">Resilience / recoverability</span> | <span lang="ja">障害の波及を抑え、処理を回復しやすい</span><span lang="en">Limit failure propagation and recover work</span> | <span lang="ja">失敗を分離して記録し、再試行・再開を管理する</span><span lang="en">Isolate and record failures; manage retries and resumption</span> |
| <span lang="ja">応答性</span><span lang="en">Responsiveness</span> | <span lang="ja">長時間処理や過負荷による応答の停滞を抑える</span><span lang="en">Limit response delays from long-running work and overload</span> | <span lang="ja">受付と完了を分け、待機量と並行実行数を制御する</span><span lang="en">Separate acceptance from completion; bound pending and concurrent work</span> |
| <span lang="ja">機能拡張・変更の柔軟性</span><span lang="en">Extensibility / flexibility</span> | <span lang="ja">部品の追加・変更の影響を限定しやすい</span><span lang="en">Limit the impact of adding or changing components</span> | <span lang="ja">メッセージの契約を保ち、各部品の処理と実行時期を分離する</span><span lang="en">Preserve message contracts while separating component processing and timing</span> |
| <span lang="ja">資源効率・運用コスト</span><span lang="en">Resource efficiency / cost</span> | <span lang="ja">待機中の資源占有や過剰な常時配備を減らせる</span><span lang="en">Reduce resources held while waiting and excessive standing capacity</span> | <span lang="ja">非ブロッキングな実行と負荷に応じた資源配分を組み合わせる</span><span lang="en">Combine non-blocking execution with demand-dependent resource allocation</span> |

<span lang="ja">非同期化すると、処理の順序や完了の確認、データの整合性、再試行に伴う重複実行など、管理すべき事項が増えます。これらの制御を業務処理ごとに実装すると、処理間で方式が異なり、システム全体で一貫した動作を保つことが難しくなります。</span><span lang="en">Asynchronous processing introduces additional concerns: ordering, completion tracking, data consistency, and duplicate execution during retries. Implementing these controls separately for each business process leads to different conventions and makes consistent system-wide behavior harder to maintain.</span>

<span lang="ja">Textus/CNCFでは、CMLで定義したモデルとCNCFの標準機能を使って業務処理を構成すると、その処理が共通の実行機構へ接続されます。ティアとコンポーネントの分担、メッセージによる連携、ジョブ管理、資源管理、障害対応がこの実行経路で働くため、開発者が業務処理ごとに非同期制御を組み立てる必要を減らせます。通常の開発では業務のモデルと処理に集中しながら、実行基盤によるリアクティブ性の支援を受けられます。技術的に難しい制御を基盤が引き受け、標準的な作法に沿う実装へ適用することが、このアーキテクチャの要点です。</span><span lang="en">Business processing built with CML models and standard CNCF facilities connects to shared execution mechanisms. Tier and component responsibilities, message-based communication, Job management, resource management, and failure handling operate along this execution path, reducing the need to construct asynchronous controls for each business process. In ordinary development, developers can concentrate on business models and logic while receiving reactive support from the runtime. Having the infrastructure take responsibility for technically demanding controls and apply them to implementations following standard conventions is a central feature of this architecture.</span>

## Relating the Four Characteristics to Quality Attributes｜四つの特性と品質属性を関連付ける

<span lang="en">The Reactive Manifesto identifies responsiveness, resilience, elasticity, and message-driven communication as interrelated characteristics. Textus/CNCF aims to return a result, acceptance state, or failure within an appropriate time despite changing load or partial failures. This requires a path for admission, execution, and outcome inspection, rather than asynchronous execution alone. Reference: The Reactive Manifesto (https://www.reactivemanifesto.org/).</span><span lang="ja">リアクティブ宣言は、応答性、耐障害性、弾力性、メッセージ駆動を相互に関連する四つの特性として整理しています。Textus/CNCFでは、負荷の変動や部分的な障害があっても、要求に対して適切な時間で結果、受付状態、失敗を返せることを目指します。単に処理を非同期化するだけでなく、その処理を受け入れ、実行し、結果を確認できる経路を設計します。参考：リアクティブ宣言（https://www.reactivemanifesto.org/）。</span>

<span lang="en">Message-driven communication reduces temporal dependencies so that load and failures can be managed separately. Textus/CNCF distinguishes requests, facts, and execution management through Commands, Events, and Jobs.</span><span lang="ja">メッセージ駆動は、処理間の時間的な依存を減らし、負荷や障害を分離して扱うための構成です。Textus/CNCFでは、Command、Event、Jobで要求、発生した事実、実行管理を区別します。</span>

<span lang="en">Using the benefits of asynchronous architecture also requires preserving consistency and security, and making separated processing observable and testable. The following mapping covers these controls and organizes combinations of Textus/CNCF mechanisms through ten quality perspectives.</span><span lang="ja">非同期な構成の利点を活かすには、データ整合性やセキュリティを保ち、分離した処理を観測・検証できることも必要です。以下では、こうした制御を含め、Textus/CNCFの技術の組合せを十の品質属性から整理します。</span>

## Quality Attributes and Their Supporting Combinations｜品質属性と技術の組合せの対応

<span lang="en">The following tables connect the quality effects introduced above to specific Textus/CNCF mechanisms, including applicability conditions and verification points. Subsequent sections explain how these mechanisms work together along the execution path.</span><span lang="ja">次の表は、導入で示した品質への効果をTextus/CNCFの具体的な機構に対応付け、成立条件と確認点を示します。後続の節では、その機構が実行経路でどう連携するかを説明します。</span>

